# Build context for the container image service in vercel.json.
#
# The `api` (gateway) service declares `"root": "./"` and builds
# `Dockerfile.vercel`, so its build context is the repository root. It has to be:
# services/go.mod replaces the platform module with a relative path
# (../packages/go/platform), so the image must carry both Go modules. Without this
# file the context would also include node_modules and every build artefact, which
# would be uploaded on every deploy.
#
# Everything below is either unrelated to a Go build or must never enter an image.

.git
.github
.vercel
.wrangler
node_modules
.output
dist
coverage

# Secrets and local configuration: an image must never carry them.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Web app and the assets it builds from, plus material the Go images do not use.
src
public
docs
supabase
tests
scripts
packages/api-contracts
*.log
